Expected elements: present

Every must-show is on the page: an identity bar with a chain-targeting `← demo` exit (y=31), four dense panes, the Data row as the transaction pane's first labelled row (badge "Synthetic demo data", y=205, with prose that agrees with it), Code with line 32 marked, a seven-frame call trace, CALL TRACE / EVENT LOG as one tab strip with Call Trace open, Values as a pane below it rather than a third tab, bidirectional stepping, and a scrubber whose 25px-of-255px fill (9.8%) matches 128/1,315. Nothing forbidden is present. It reads as a tool.

It does not read as *this* product's tool. The design system's brand accent #4f46e5 occurs in exactly four places on the whole screen, and all four are hyperlinks; every debugger-native state mark uses a cyan or blue the brand does not own. "You are here" is drawn five ways, including a doubled rule under iteration chip 3.

On the changes: (a) landed — the current arm takes the position ink — but the reader meets four gutter states in three inks with no key. (b) landed; COST · MANA holds one line. (c) did not land as an inferable rule: "128 / 1,315" and "88000 / 200000" are the same construction formatted two ways. (d) as found: the fade is one 23px row in the Code pane only; the transaction pane clips at full ink.

Fixes: give the debugger's own state marks the brand accent; unify the current-marker primitive.

Rating: 6/10

